nk":true,"_score_share_shrink":76.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.024068452480234846,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":59.9,"_gate_insider_own":0.0030500002,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":2.0,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"ON Semiconductor Corporation provides intelligent sensing and power solutions in Hong Kong, Singapore, the United Kingdom, the United States, and internationally. It operates through three segments: Power Solutions Group, Analog and Mixed-Signal Group, and Intelligent Sensing Group. The Power Solutions Group segment offers discrete, module, and integrated semiconductor devices designed to enable power conversion, including power switching, signal conditioning, and circuit protection technologies. Its Analog and Mixed-Signal Group segment designs and develops analog and mixed-signal solutions, including power management, sensor interface, connectivity, and standard products for automotive, industrial automation, AI data centers, computing, and mobile end markets. The Intelligent Sensing Group segment develops complementary metal-oxide-semiconductor image sensors, image signal processors, short-wave infrared sensors, and other products, as well as photon-counting technologies, including single-photon avalanche diode arrays and silicon photomultiplier devices for depth sensing, factory automation, safety systems, and robotics industries. ON Semiconductor Corporation was incorporated in 1992 and is headquartered in Scottsdale, Arizona.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Hassane S. El-Khoury | President, CEO & Director | Age 45 | Compensation: $1.2M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 22K people. Revenue per employee of $265K ranks in the below the sector median among Technology peers, with revenue growing 7%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $63K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $6K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 5\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["ON Semiconductor Corporation is a large-cap technology business with a $27.7B market cap on $6.0B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -10% over the past three years and +6% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 18% against a 11% cost of capital, a 8-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it, with gross margins sitting at 35%.","The business throws off $1.4B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 24 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 14.54\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.6\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and thin 1.2\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 5.0% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.1\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Technology peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (10.1% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Heavy insider selling (net $13.3M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-13300647.11},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 7% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Elevated sector volatility (38% annualized) adds uncertainty","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"ON Semiconductor (ON) Stock Fair Value Edges Lower As Analysts Cut Targets","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/semiconductor-stock-fair-value-edges-171319953.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794503599.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.915,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Wall Street Analysts Believe ON Semiconductor Corp. (ON) Could Rally 29.15%: Here's is How to Trade","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/wall-street-analysts-believe-semiconductor-135502146.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794491702.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.605,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Here's Why ON Semiconductor Corp. (ON) is a Strong Momentum Stock","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3028677/here-s-why-on-semiconductor-corp-on-is-a-strong-momentum-stock?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Czacks_education_momentum_score-3028677","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794491403.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.511,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"EliteS